# Marktplaats listings

Use Playwright MCP (`user-playwright`) on the seller’s already-logged-in session. Never ask for or type the password. Cursor’s built-in browser is a different session — do not use it for this. If the header is not **Hello World Cards**, stop and ask the user to log in.

Do not post a card that is `concept` or not in stock. Do not change prices on other live ads.

## Chat triggers — do this immediately

- **Go live / list {card}:** pre-flight → fill the form → **stop and wait** for the user to check it → only then publish. After they confirm, drop `concept` and set `marktplaatsUrl`. Shop shows **View on Marktplaats**. Then also post the card to Vinted per **`vinted-listings`** (same title/photos/price, English description) and set `vintedUrl`. A card never goes to Vinted while still `concept`.
- **Change price / lower price / set price to €X** (for a card): follow **cms-inventory** (seed + D1 push, or CMS pull) then **always** update Marktplaats (Vraagprijs **and** Bieden vanaf) when the card has a `marktplaatsUrl`, and Vinted when it has a `vintedUrl`. See **Shop vs Marktplaats price** below (Vinted keeps the plain shop price, no cent trick).
- **{card} is gereserveerd / reserved / sold but still on its way / sold on Vinted, waiting for the payout** (a sale whose money has not come in yet): **shop first** (`reserved: true`, `soldAt`, the sale `price`, both URLs kept), then set the Marktplaats ad to **Gereserveerd**, then the Vinted listing (nothing to do when the sale was on Vinted). Nothing is deleted yet. See **Reserved** below.
- **{card} is sold for €X** (or “sold for X euros”, “the money is in”): **shop first**, then delete the Marktplaats ad under the reason that matches where it sold, then delete the Vinted ad too if `vintedUrl` is set. See Sold below. A reserved card takes the same path; only the deletes are new.
- **Delete the listing / not in stock / just take it down** (not a sale): **shop first** (`concept: true`, no URL, stays in the shop as **Not yet available to buy**), then delete the Marktplaats ad as **not** sold, then delete the Vinted ad too if `vintedUrl` is set.

Until a card is live it stays `concept: true` with no listing URL. A card is `reserved: true` from the moment it sells until the money is in, and `sold: true` after that — never `sold` while a payout is still pending.

## Live CMS (D1)

See **`.cursor/rules/cms-inventory.mdc`** for the full seed ↔ D1 sync contract. Short version for price/listing work:

1. Chat-driven change → edit seed → **`npm run cms:sync-products:remote`** → Marktplaats if listed.
2. Admin CMS change → live site is already updated → **`npm run cms:pull-products:remote`** to refresh seed → Marktplaats if price/listing changed.

Never treat the seed file alone as “live”.

## Listing URLs

Products store the **seller view** URL after publish:

- View: `https://www.marktplaats.nl/seller/view/{itemId}` (e.g. `m2436896724`)
- Edit: `https://www.marktplaats.nl/plaats/{itemId}/edit` — same `{itemId}`

Use `marktplaatsEditUrlFromListingUrl(product.marktplaatsUrl)` from `app/services/marktplaats.ts` to jump straight to the edit form (faster than seller view → **Wijzig**).

**Fallback:** if direct navigation to the edit URL fails (login wall, 404, wrong page), open `marktplaatsUrl` on seller view and click **Wijzig** (`/plaats/{itemId}/edit` link), or find the ad under **Mijn advertenties**.

## Shop vs Marktplaats price

- **Shop** keeps the clean whole-euro price the user asked for (e.g. `€100`, `€95`).
- **Marktplaats Vraagprijs** is always **one cent less** than the shop — psychological pricing so listings look slightly cheaper (shop `€100` → Marktplaats `99,99`). Only on Marktplaats; never change the shop price to match.
- Use `marktplaatsVraagprijsFromShop(product.price)` from `app/services/price.ts` for the **Vraagprijs** textbox (`99,99` format). Examples: `€100` → `99,99`, `€95` → `94,99`, `€65` → `64,99`.
- Do **not** retroactively reprice every live ad when this rule changes; apply on the next price change or new listing.

### Change price on Marktplaats

1. Shop first — seed file + **D1 sync** (see **Live CMS (D1)**); update tests if they assert `price`.
2. If the product has `marktplaatsUrl`, navigate to `marktplaatsEditUrlFromListingUrl(marktplaatsUrl)` (fallback: seller view → **Wijzig**).
3. Set **Vraagprijs** to `marktplaatsVraagprijsFromShop(shop price)` — not the shop amount.
4. Set **Bieden vanaf** to `marktplaatsBiedenVanafFromShop(shop price)` — see **Bieden**.
5. **Opslaan**. Confirm the seller view shows the Marktplaats price (e.g. `€ 99,99`).

## Always (form)

- **Photos:** slab front first, slab back second. Upload `public` + `product.images` (`*_front.jpg` then `*_back.jpg`).
- **Category:** title → **Vind categorie** → Verzamelkaartspellen | Pokémon (Hobby en Vrije tijd).
- **Kenmerken:** Zo goed als nieuw, Type Losse kaart, Foil on.
- **Levering:** Ophalen of Verzenden. Pakketgrootte **Brievenbuspakje** (never Klein pakket).
- **Prijs:** Vraagprijs = `marktplaatsVraagprijsFromShop(shop price)` (one cent below shop). **Bieden toestaan** on, **Bieden vanaf** = `marktplaatsBiedenVanafFromShop(shop price)` (e.g. `84,99`). See **Bieden**.
- **Adverteren:** **Gratis** only. Never Plus/Premium unless asked.

## Bieden

Every live ad has bidding on (rolled out 14 September 2026). The numbers come from `marktplaatsBiddingFromShop(shop price)` / `marktplaatsBiedenVanafFromShop(shop price)` in `app/services/price.ts` — never improvise them:

- **Floor** (`counterOffer`): shop price minus **€5** under €100, minus **€10** from €100 up, rounded up to a whole €5. This is the lowest price we ever sell at, and it is always a round number.
- **Bieden vanaf** (`minimumBid`): one €5 step under the floor, less one cent — the same trick as the Vraagprijs. Marktplaats shows it publicly on the ad as `Vanaf € 84,99`, so it is the buyer's anchor.

| Shop | Vraagprijs | Bieden vanaf | Floor / tegenbod |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| €50 | 49,99 | 39,99 | 45 |
| €65 | 64,99 | 54,99 | 60 |
| €95 | 94,99 | 84,99 | 90 |
| €100 | 99,99 | 84,99 | 90 |
| €110 | 109,99 | 94,99 | 100 |
| €130 | 129,99 | 114,99 | 120 |

**On the form** (place and edit): toggle `[data-testid="syi-bidding-switch"]` (**Bieden toestaan**), which reveals the **Bieden vanaf** textbox `input[name="price.minimumBidPrice"]`; fill it with the `84,99`-style string. After **Opslaan** the seller view shows `Biedingen … Vanaf € 84,99`.

**Responding to a bid** (Marktplaats messages: Accepteren / Afwijzen / Tegenbod):

- Bid **≥ floor** → accept.
- Bid **< floor** (usually exactly the Bieden vanaf amount) → **tegenbod at the floor**, once, with a message like: `Bedankt voor je bod! €85 is net te weinig, maar voor €90 is hij voor jou — dat is echt het minste wat ik kan doen.` The floor is one step above their bid, so there is no round number left to "meet in the middle" on.
- Never go under the floor, never split the difference, never a second tegenbod. If they walk, they walk (see the no-price-drops rule).
- A price change moves the floor and the Bieden vanaf with it — update both on the edit form.

## Place an ad

1. Draft title + description from the frozen references **before** opening the form.
2. **Plaats advertentie** → paste title → **Vind categorie** → Pokémon → **Verder**.
3. Photos, kenmerken, levering, prijs (Vraagprijs **and** Bieden toestaan + Bieden vanaf), Gratis (defaults above).
4. Description last, in `.RichTextEditor-module-editorInput`. Type it — see Description. Never `fill()` or set `innerHTML`.
5. **Stop.** Do **not** click **Plaats je advertentie** (or **Plaats advertentie** on the last step). Tell the user the form is ready and wait until they say it looks good (or ask for a fix).
6. Only after they confirm: **Plaats je advertentie**. Copy `marktplaatsSellerViewUrl(itemId)` onto the product; drop `concept`. Update tests if they assert concept/URL.

## Reserved — sold, still on its way

A card is reserved when it has been sold but the buyer has not received it yet and the money has not been paid out (Vinted holds the payment until the buyer confirms; a Marktplaats buyer may still be paying). It is off the market but not settled, so it is neither `concept` nor `sold`.

### Shop first

In `app/cms/seed-products.ts` on that card (or the local admin: status **Reserved**):

- `reserved: true`
- `soldAt: 'YYYY-MM-DD'` — the day it sold; today unless the user says otherwise
- `price: '€X'` — the actual sale amount, when the user gives one (the dashboard reads revenue from `price`)
- keep `marktplaatsUrl` and `vintedUrl`; never `sold: true` yet

The shop keeps the card but hides its price: the card in the grid and the button on its page both say **This card is reserved** instead. The card leaves the Vinted relist tab and the price suggestions on its own, and the relist API refuses it. Sync per **cms-inventory** and update tests that assert the card's price or status.

### Then the ads — mark, do not delete

- **Marktplaats:** open `marktplaatsUrl` on seller view (fallback: **Mijn advertenties**) and switch the ad to **Gereserveerd**. The ad stays up with that label; deleting it comes later, with the money.
- **Vinted:** sold **on Vinted** → nothing to do, Vinted has already marked the listing sold and holds the payout. Sold **elsewhere** → mark the Vinted listing reserved (the seller's reserve option on the listing page), so nobody buys it twice.

If Playwright is not logged in, still update the shop first, then ask the user to log in for the ads.

### When the money is in

The user says the card **is sold** (“sold for €X”, “the money is in”): follow **Sold for €X — shop first** below. `soldAt` and `price` are already set — check the amount — so what changes is `sold: true`, dropping `reserved` and both URLs, and the deletes: the Marktplaats ad under the reason that matches where it sold (see **Sold / delete an ad**), and the Vinted listing unless Vinted already closed it.

## Sold / delete an ad

Marktplaats delete is an **in-page** choice, not a native `alert`. After **Verwijder**, click:

The choice reports **where the card sold**, not whether it sold:

- **Verkocht via Marktplaats** if the sale was on Marktplaats
- **Niet verkocht via Marktplaats** if it sold on Vinted (or anywhere else), and also when we are only taking the ad down

Do not `dialog.accept()`. Open `marktplaatsUrl` on seller view (fallback: **Mijn advertenties** if the URL is missing). Confirm it is gone (410 / missing from the ads list).

### Sold for €X — shop first

In `app/cms/seed-products.ts` on that card (or the local admin: status **Sold**):

- `sold: true`
- `soldAt: 'YYYY-MM-DD'` (today, or the day it sold if the card was reserved first)
- `price: '€X'` — **actual sale amount** (dashboard revenue reads `price`)
- remove `marktplaatsUrl`, `vintedUrl`, `concept`, and `reserved`
- leave `images` alone: once the sale has settled, the dev server keeps one small front photo (`…-front-sold.webp`, media folder **Sold**) and removes the back photo, the full-size originals and the branded ad in `public/ads` on its own (see **cms-inventory**). Its rewrite of the seed files is part of the diff to commit.

That hides it from the shop (`isShopListed`) and keeps it on the dashboard, on the admin's **Sold** tab. Then delete the Marktplaats ad under the reason that matches where it sold — **Verkocht via Marktplaats** only when the sale was on Marktplaats, **Niet verkocht via Marktplaats** when it sold on Vinted. Update `test/products.test.ts` (and any catalog assertions) so the card is no longer expected in the shop.

If Playwright is not logged in, still update the shop first, then ask the user to log in so the ad can be deleted.

### Delete without a sale

`concept: true`, remove `marktplaatsUrl` and `vintedUrl`, do **not** set `sold`. Then **Niet verkocht via Marktplaats**.

## Title

`{Name} {number} {variant} - {Grader} {grade} - {Set}`

Examples: `Zorua 140/086 AR - BGS 9.5 - White Flare Japanese`, `Arceus V Full Art 165/172 - PSA 9 - Brilliant Stars`.

## Description (Lexical editor)

Copy the frozen reference ads below. Do not depend on Marktplaats URLs — those ads disappear when a card sells.

Click the editor, then:

- **Enter** between major sections (new paragraph = visible blank line)
- **Shift+Enter** inside a section (Details bullets, 📦 then 💬, ⭐ then the combine line)
- **Cmd+B** for bold: the `Mooie …` phrase, **Details:**, **Bekijk ook onze andere advertenties!**. Bold grade / subgrades / pop only when they are a selling point (Zorua).

**Blank line between every major section.** Details bullets stay tight.

The 📦 line is one line, fixed wording, in every ad: shipping or pickup possible, then that shipping is at the buyer's own risk and we are not liable for damage or loss in transit — no line break before the own-risk sentence.

### Pop

Only mention pop when it is **low** (tens, like Zorua’s 20): intro `Lage **pop** van **{n}**.` and `• Pop: {n}`.

Skip pop when it is high / irrelevant (hundreds or thousands — Charizard has none). If unsure, omit.

